q
1 0 0 1 85.2 544.5 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 76 Tm 17.5 TL /F1 11.5 Tf .14902 .141176 .113725 rg (I am a working musician. I have spent my life around stringed instruments, and here is) Tj T* (what my instrument kept telling me: ) Tj /F2 11.5 Tf (nothing in physics works by "attraction" the) Tj T* (way these teachers describe it.) Tj /F1 11.5 Tf ( In the physical world, like charges repel. Nothing in) Tj T* (nature reaches out and drags outcomes toward you because you pictured them hard) Tj T* (enough.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 85.2 446 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 76 Tm 17.5 TL /F1 11.5 Tf .14902 .141176 .113725 rg (But something else ) Tj /F3 11.5 Tf (is) Tj /F1 11.5 Tf ( real, and I could demonstrate it with two guitars. Strike a string) Tj T* (on one guitar, and the same string on a second guitar nearby will begin to vibrate \227) Tj T* (untouched. Nothing pulled it. Nothing forced it. It responded, because it was ) Tj /F2 11.5 Tf (tuned to) Tj T* (the same note) Tj /F1 11.5 Tf (. Musicians and physicists call this ) Tj /F3 11.5 Tf (sympathetic resonance) Tj /F1 11.5 Tf (, and it is) Tj T* (observable, repeatable, and about as mystical as a tuning fork.) Tj T* ET
Q
